# bible.db WAS a pure build artifact, regenerable from assets/. It no longer is:
# it now carries the English translation, which cannot be rebuilt from the
# Amharic source. It is tracked deliberately, and committed at milestones rather
# than on every change so the history doesn't fill with 15 MB blobs.

# SQLite sidecars, never committed. The db is in WAL mode while translators run
# in parallel, and a committed non-empty -wal would be silently INVISIBLE to the
# reader: store.py opens with immutable=1, which tells SQLite that locking is
# unnecessary and makes it ignore the WAL. Verses would exist in the file and not
# appear in the app. tools/seal_db.py checkpoints and clears WAL mode before a
# milestone commit.
src/ebible/data/bible.db-wal
src/ebible/data/bible.db-shm
